## THE COMMISSION
Add the missing red-proof cells for the eight tickets above, test-only, each proven red against a named mutant of the product and green on main, and regenerate the test-count file ONCE at the end. The product owner's standing rule (merge-once-tested; a gate before every merge) applies: you build, a tier-2 gate measures, Tuesday opens the PR and lands it.

## THE WORK (the order is the order)
1. **Pins, baseline, worktrees.** Record `date`, two `uptime` reads 4 s apart, `node -v`, `npm -v` (CI uses node 24; if your npm major differs from the one that wrote the lock, expect churn, and never commit `package-lock.json`: the diff must not show it), the main sha, the refs list `git for-each-ref --format='%(refname) %(objectname)'` to `session-tools/b588/logs/refs-before.txt`, `git worktree list` before, the root checkout's `status --porcelain | wc -l` (drafter read 34). Create `worktrees/b588-fix` with `git worktree add -b b588/nexusai-n1-test-cells <path> <main sha>` (the object is local; if it is not, ONE explicit-refspec fetch into the git directory only, never `--prune`, never a bare fetch; assert `rev-parse HEAD` = the main sha and a clean tree) and `worktrees/b588-mut` with `git worktree add --detach <path> <main sha>` (the MUTANT tree: nothing in it is ever committed or pushed). `npm ci --no-audit --no-fund` in both (or, if you find `node_modules` can be shared by symlink without jest or `require` resolving the wrong tree, say which you used). **Baseline:** in `b588-fix`, before any edit, `npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2` through the jest lock (STANDING LINE 9): `VERDICT: PASS` with tests 4971 and suites 305 or STOP naming the red cells (do not build on a red main).
2. **Per ticket (the loop).** (a) Re-read the ticket and the file at main. (b) Write the cell(s) in `b588-fix`. (c) **Green on main:** `npx jest --maxWorkers=2 <the file>` through the lock in `b588-fix`: your new cells pass, every old cell in the file still passes (quote the `Tests:` line before and after: old count + new count = new total). **A new cell that is RED on main is a PRODUCT DEFECT: drop that cell, do not touch product code, record it under FINDINGS (cell text, the output) and mark the ticket "cell not shippable" in STATUS.** (d) **Red-first by mutant:** copy the new test file into `b588-mut`, write the mutant over the product file there (from `git show <main sha>:<path>` with a one-line `sed`/`python3 -I` edit, asserting the anchor matched exactly once), run the same file through the lock, record RED (which cells, the failing assertion) and the same file with the mutant's anchor restored from `git show` (never `checkout`, `reset` or `stash`): GREEN again. A cell that kills none of its ticket's named mutants is returned: say so, do not ship it. (e) ONE commit in `b588-fix` for the ticket: message names the ticket, the gate finding, the mutant(s) and the rows killed, "test-only, no product file", trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; no person's name; no card id.
3. **Counts, once, last.** After the eight commits: the whole suite through the lock: `npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2 --update-counts` (the `--` is load-bearing, RD-561), read `VERDICT: PASS`; then `git diff` of the counts file: `tests` = 4971 + the number of cells you added (assert equal by program: the sum of each file's Before/After `Tests:` deltas), `suites` = 305 (+1 only if you added the one optional new file), `_updated` changed, nothing else. Commit it alone: "counts regenerated once for N1 (tests <old> -> <new>, suites <old> -> <new>)". Then run `npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2` once more WITHOUT `--update-counts` and read `VERDICT: PASS` against the committed file. **Never run `--update-counts` in the middle**; the intermediate commits are red against the counts file by design (only the head is gated).
4. **Property checks, push.** See THE PROPERTY CHECKS. Push exactly one branch.

### Ticket rows (what to build, what kills it)

**Row 1, RD-825.** Add to `NOT_ADMIN_USERS` the rows `{ user: { role: ['admin'] } }` and `{ user: { role: ['viewer', 'admin'] } }` (labels in the file's style). They ride the existing `test.each` (P9): every `NOT_PLAIN` value must come back `null`, and a plain one must come back as the allow-list. Mutants (in `b588-mut`, `healthProjection.js:50`): **MadminArray** `req.user.role === 'admin'` -> `String(req.user.role) === 'admin'` (a one-element array stringifies to `admin`); **MadminIncl** -> `[].concat(req.user.role).includes('admin')`. Expected: row 1 red under both, row 2 red under MadminIncl only (state which row kills which; a row that kills neither is dropped).

**Row 2, RD-860.** In the print-window describe add one cell: `run('</title><script>window.__rd778=1</script>')`; assert (i) the written text contains the escaped breakout inside `<title>` (`&lt;/title&gt;&lt;script&gt;` ... as the shipped `escapeHtml` produces it; read the exact form from the control cell), (ii) the parsed document has NO `script` element and `doc.title` equals the payload text, (iii) the CONTROL cell's ordinary title still reads exactly as before (leave it). Mutant (in `b588-mut`, `static/js/chart-details.js:556`): `<title>${escapeHtml(title)}</title>` -> `<title>${title}</title>` at that ONE site (the `<h1>` site stays escaped). **Premise to prove first:** the file's existing cells, including the `<img onerror>` one, stay GREEN under that mutant (the ticket's "16 cells green"; quote the file's count), and the new cell goes RED.

**Row 3, RD-877.** (a) **Boundary row**: a printer-log row whose `Total_Sheets_Used` equals the threshold of `page_count_above` must NOT be returned by that template (strict `>`). Plant the row in the test's OWN database (the test already opens `sqlite3.Database(path.join(dataDir, 'printer_logs.db'))` for its reference reads; build the row from an existing seeded row's shape, change nothing else); the rows returned for threshold T exclude it and include a row at T+1 (control, so the cell cannot pass on an empty result). (b) **Gate cells**: in the `RD-836 C` block (the viewer/admin harness, `:463`), a signed-in VIEWER posting `/api/validate-condition` with `saveToDatabase` of `'true'` (a string) and of `1` is refused (403) and the risk-condition store is byte-unchanged; with `false`, `0`, `''` the route answers WITHOUT saving (status as the file's existing no-save control, store unchanged). Read `server.js:6947-7037` first: if a truthy non-boolean is NOT saved by the later save branch (`:7037`), the M14b mutant has no effect and you say so with the output rather than ship a cell that cannot go red. Mutants: **M10** `riskSqlTemplates.js:127` `Total_Sheets_Used > ?` -> `Total_Sheets_Used >= ?`; **M14b** `server.js:6950` `if (saveToDatabase && !(await requireAdminFor(req, res))) return;` -> `if (saveToDatabase === true && !(await requireAdminFor(req, res))) return;`. Each is run alone (two mutant runs).

**Row 4, RD-865 (decided by measurement; the pin is a hash, not a copy of the text).** Compute, in `b588-fix`, `sha256` and `.length` of `require('./model-config').MODEL_CONFIG.systemPrompt` at main. **If the sha256 starts `f36881dd` and the length is 9956** (the gate's recorded value, RELAYED from the gate 28 report: "prompt sha256 f36881dd... len 9956 equal (= the board's approved r1 attachment + card 2's two fixes, byte for byte)") add ONE cell to the wording describe: `sha(PROMPT)` equals the FULL 64-hex literal you computed and `PROMPT.length` equals 9956, with a comment: a deliberate change to the approved wording updates this literal and cites the word pack in the commit. A prompt-copy fixture is not needed and not allowed (no new file, no copy of the product text into the tests). **If either differs: STOP** (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with both values and a one-line diff summary by length and first differing line number): pinning a text that is not the approved one is the product owner's call. Mutants (in `b588-mut`, `model-config.js`, the `SYSTEM_PROMPT` literal at `:44`): **M865a** append one sentence at the end of the prompt (every `toContain` phrase survives); **M865b** change ONE letter inside a sentence that no RULES or KEPT phrase contains. Premise to prove: BOTH mutants leave the old wording cells green (22 of the file's cells are non-discriminating per the gate), and the new cell goes red under both.

